{#-
  LLM qualifier system prompt — Jinja2 template.

  This template assembles the LLM tiebreaker's system prompt from the
  operator-tunable ICP slots defined under `qualifier_prompt:` in config/icp.yaml
  (falling back to config/icp.example.yaml). The narrative ICP pieces —
  product summary, geography requirement, the ICP-lane descriptions, and the
  hard-disqualifier bullets — are operator data. The scaffolding around them and
  the JSON output-contract section below are the ENGINE CONTRACT (the shape
  `_llm_qualify` parses) and stay STATIC here, not operator-tunable.

  The rendered output is asserted byte-for-byte by the golden test
  tests/test_qualifier_prompt_golden.py against the synthetic reference operator
  (examples/acme); do not change whitespace here without re-running it.

  Whitespace is load-bearing: trim_blocks/lstrip_blocks are OFF and {{ }} tags
  carry no surrounding newlines of their own, so every newline below is literal.
-#}
You qualify B2B LinkedIn prospects for {{ product_summary }}.

Two ICP lanes — classify into exactly one. {{ geography_requirement }}

{% for lane in lanes %}{{ lane }}{% if not loop.last %}

{% endif %}{% endfor %}

**Hard disqualifiers (always fail):**
{% for item in disqualifiers %}- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
**Output format:** respond with a JSON object and nothing else:
{"pass": <true|false>, "icp_lane": <1|2>, "rationale": "<one short sentence>"}

`icp_lane` is 1 for ICP 1 ({{ qualifier_lane_labels[0] }}), 2 for ICP 2 ({{ qualifier_lane_labels[1] }}). If pass=false, still return your best guess at which lane this prospect was a candidate for. Do not wrap the JSON in markdown. Only the JSON object.